{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right|=\\dfrac{1}{4}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left|\\left( (-1)^{n+2}\\dfrac{(n+2)^4}{4^{n+1}} \\right)\\left( \\dfrac{4^n}{(-1)^{n+1}(n+1)^4}\\right)\\right|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\dfrac{(n+2)^4\\cdot4^n}{4^{n+1}\\cdot(n+1)^4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}~\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\left(\\dfrac{n+2}{n+1}\\right)^4\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{4}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire process.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Since the limit, $\\dfrac{1}{4}$, is less than $1$, the ratio test tells us that the series converges.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$a_n={(-1)^{n+1}\\dfrac{(n+1)^4}{4^n}}$\n\n**1) Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right|$.**\n\n$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left| \\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n} \\right|=$ [[☃ input-number 1]]\n\n**2) Based on your answer, what does the ratio test say about $S=\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"input-number 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerType":"number","inexact":false,"maxError":0.1,"simplify":"required","size":"normal","value":0.25},"static":false,"type":"input-number","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"The series converges